      "title": "1st Chieftain of the Dúnedain",
      "house": "House of Isildur",
      "realm": "Dúnedain of the North",
      "born": "1938",
      "died": "2106",
      "image": "assets/aranarth.png",
      "bio": "Aranarth was the son of Arvedui, last King of Arthedain, and Fíriel of Gondor, making him a descendant of both Isildur and Anárion. After the Witch-king of Angmar destroyed Arthedain and Arvedui was lost at sea, Aranarth became heir to the fallen North-kingdom. Though Angmar was defeated soon after, the northern Dúnedain were too few and scattered to restore their realm, so Aranarth took the title Chieftain of the Dúnedain. His line continued in secrecy, with the heirs of the Chieftains raised in Rivendell and the heirlooms of Arnor kept in Elrond’s care.",
      "order": 5
    },
